  "number": 5921,
  "title": "Read live region messages without article and group role words",
  "body": "> Screen readers say \"article\" and \"group\" before every new message and each of its lines.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed screen readers saying \"article\" and \"group\" before new messages and each of their lines in the live region, in PR [#5921](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5921), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe live region copy of a message and its attachments were `<article>`, and each line a `<div>` or `<p>` (\"group\" on Windows), so Narrator read \"article, group, Bot WC said:, group, …\". Articles are now `<div>`, and containers and lines inside the message are `role=\"none\"`; text, `aria-atomic`, buttons and inputs are unchanged.\n\n## Design\n\n- `role=\"none\"` on lines rather than `<p>`/`<span>` (still \"group\") or one text node (rewrites every renderer); the `aria-atomic` element itself must stay in the tree.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `LiveRegionActivity.tsx`: `<article aria-atomic>` → `<div aria-atomic>`, lines `role=\"none\"`; props typed with `InferReactProps`\n- `LiveRegionAttachments.tsx`, `LiveRegionSuggestedActions.tsx`: wrappers and paragraphs `role=\"none\"`\n- `AdaptiveCardAttachment.js`, `RichCardAttachment.js`, core `AttachmentForScreenReader/*Attachment.js`: `<article>` → `<div>`, lines and containers `role=\"none\"`\n- `ACCESSIBILITY.md`: custom screen reader renderers should do the same\n- `accessibility/liveRegion/noRoleWords.html`: asserts text, `aria-atomic`, a generic message and only buttons in its accessibility tree; snapshot 1 shows the live region copy with no role words\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n\n",
